---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { locales } from '../data/locales';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us - PixoraScreen"
  description="Learn more about PixoraScreen, our mission, features, and the premium technology stack behind our fullscreen utilities."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  lang={locales.en.lang}
  locale="en"
>
  <section class="site-shell py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">Our Story</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-5xl font-semibold leading-[0.95] text-balance text-ink md:text-6xl">About Us.</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-body text-balance">
        PixoraScreen is a collection of premium fullscreen utilities designed to transform any display into a dedicated workspace, diagnostic tool, or ambient surface.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-hairline bg-canvas">
    <article class="rich-article site-shell max-w-3xl py-12 md:py-16">
      <h2>Who's Behind PixoraScreen</h2>
      <p>
        PixoraScreen is built and maintained by <strong>Gyanranjan Patra</strong>, a BTech graduate in Information Technology. The idea started from a personal habit: keeping an ambient background running while coding or doing deep work, since a calm, moving visual holds focus better than a blank desktop or a stray browser tab pulling attention away.
      </p>
      <p>
        That itch — wanting one fast, ad-free place to pull up an ambient screen, a color field, or a display test without wading through cluttered sites — is what turned into PixoraScreen.
      </p>

      <h2>The Mission</h2>
      <p>
        Most fullscreen utilities on the web are cluttered with invasive advertisements, tracking cookies, and laggy rendering. We built <strong>PixoraScreen</strong> as a premium, fast, and completely distraction-free alternative.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whether you are testing a gaming monitor for dead pixels, setting up a relaxing ambient screensaver for study, playing a friendly prank on a coworker, or simulating updates for video production, our tools provide a flawless, high-fidelity experience.
      </p>

      <h2>Core Features</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
        <li><strong>Pure Color Screens</strong>: Open solid colors in fullscreen for screen cleaning, light painting, or checking color reproduction.</li>
        <li><strong>Display Diagnostics</strong>: Easily check and test screens for dead pixels or burn-in with precise color shifts.</li>
        <li><strong>Ambient Screensavers</strong>: Choose from a glassmorphic flip clock, matrix rain code, particle snow, gentle rain, fireplace, or deep space.</li>
        <li><strong>Realistic Prank Screens</strong>: Convincingly replicate system upgrade screens (Windows, macOS, Ubuntu, Android), radar sweeps, or retro crash screens.</li>
        <li><strong>Keyboard Shortcuts</strong>: Fast controls block-wide (like pressing <kbd class="rounded border border-hairline px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs bg-canvas-soft">F</kbd> for fullscreen) allow rapid repeatability.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Privacy & Performance First</h2>
      <p>
        We respect your privacy. Every tool runs entirely client-side in your browser — there are no accounts, no logins, and no invasive ad trackers or third-party marketing pixels. We use privacy-respecting Google Analytics only to understand aggregate traffic patterns (which tools are popular, which pages need work), never to build individual profiles or sell data. All animation frames render smoothly with specialized canvas and CSS layout logic, remaining performant across laptops, tablets, smart TVs, and mobile devices.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
